0	section	Talking to Sergeant Hudson
1	line	Player	I've found some interesting things that you should know about.
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	There's a good chance we've found them ourselves already, but let's hear them.
1	line	Player	The victim was seemingly killed by a stab wound to the heart, and it seems they were specifically targeted by the killer. Some sort of encoded message was left on them, and there were more symbols on the wall as well.
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	And?
1	line	Player	The victim was once a judge and made a fair few enemies. It's possible one of them specifically targeted him. If so, it might not be the first time. Many years ago, his wife and daughter were killed as well.
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	Yes, Betty told us that as well, but none of this gives us much to go on. As you said, he likely had multiple enemies. We need something more specific.
1	line	Player	Well, from what a neighbour overheard, the killer was likely known to the victim.
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	That's not too surprising and doesn't actually narrow things down much. He knew a lot of people, and would remember a lot more from his past.
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	Unfortunately, it doesn't seem you've really uncovered anything that will help us. Still, maybe your work will reassure Betty a bit. Now, it's time we started wrapping up here.
1	line	Player	Well, hang on... What about the local butcher?
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	What about him?
1	line	Player	An odd acting butcher who has no produce, yet did have a blood-covered knife hidden under his bed. Does that not seem a bit suspicious?
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	A blood-covered knife? We missed that...
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	Still, it's hardly proof of anything. We haven't found any real link between him and the victim, nor do we have any more information on the odd symbols.
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	However, I would say we have enough reason to take him in for questioning. I'll have the corporals arrange it...
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	Right, I think we've done all we need to here. Someone will be out soon to take care of your father's body. In the meantime, Betty, do you have anywhere else you can go?
1	line	Betty	To my uncle's south of Hosidius, but... is that it? You're not going to do anything else?
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	We'll continue our investigation back at the Shayzien Administration. We have some leads to explore and a person of interest to question further. We'll let you know if we learn anything.
1	line	Betty	And in the meantime, the killer gets to remain loose?! What if they come back?! What if I'm next?!
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	I promise you, we don't want a killer out there any longer than they need to be. We will find them, Betty. You have my word.
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	For now, if you're feeling unsafe, I can arrange for you to have some protection.
1	line	Betty	Protection? From you? I know what you people are like. Father told me more than a few stories about the 'honourable' Shayzien Constabulary...
1	line	Betty	No. You people can't protect me. I'll be better off on my own.
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	I'm sorry you feel that way. Will you at least allow me to arrange an escort to take you to your uncle's home?
1	line	Betty	No... I'll make my own way there... after I've properly said goodbye to my father.
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	If you're sure... Take care of yourself, Betty. We'll be in touch soon.
1	line	Player	Would you like me to take you to Hosidius?
1	line	Betty	No. Thank you, but I'd like some time alone. A quiet walk is the sort of thing I need. But...
1	line	Player	What is it?
1	line	Betty	I shouldn't ask any more of you... but I just don't trust the authorities to see this through. Could you meet me at my uncle's house? I want to talk through everything a bit more.
1	line	Player	Of course. It's not a problem.
1	line	Betty	Thank you. My uncle lives south of the city itself, just north west of the Tithe Farm. I'll meet you there.
1	action	end
