2	line	Betty	No. Uncle Bernard wasn't like my father, working some dangerous job. Before he retired, he was just a clerical assistant. He spent his days filing papers! He wasn't even a proper member of the army!
2	action	other
1	option	Was your uncle a big drinker?
2	line	Player	Was your uncle a big drinker?
2	line	Betty	I suppose so. He was always a big fan of wine.
2	line	Player	Would he drink with others, or alone?
2	line	Betty	Mostly alone. He liked his privacy. He'd always be happy to get a bottle or two out if he did have visitors though. He'd always insist on me or my father having at least one drink with him if we visited.
2	action	other
1	option	Have you heard of the Keystone Lodge?
2	line	Player	Have you heard of the Keystone Lodge?
2	line	Betty	Yes... It was some special group Uncle Bernard was part of. Father was a member as well. I don't really know what it was all about. Something to do with self- betterment for the good of all, I think.
2	line	Betty	It all seemed a bit silly to me, but it kept them happy, at least... until the group closed down a few months ago.
2	line	Player	Do you know why it closed?
2	line	Betty	Lack of new members apparently.
2	action	other
