0	section	Talking to the monk
1	line	Player	Hello there. I was wondering if I could ask you some questions?
1	line	Monk	Go ahead, my child.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Do you know anything about the person who lives in this house?
2	line	Player	Do you know anything about the person who lives in this house?
2	line	Monk	Ah, you mean that blaspheming dissident! He is not someone worth knowing about, but alas, I have had the misfortune of interacting with him.
2	line	Player	Okay, there's clearly a story here.
2	line	Monk	That there is, my child. I am from the nearby camp of peaceful monks. We spend our days dedicating ourselves to Saradomin, and sometimes spreading his teachings across the kingdom.
2	line	Monk	I regularly travel around here, sharing the word of our holy lord. That is what I am doing right now, in fact, and it was what I was doing when he came and confronted me.
2	line	Player	What did he confront you about?
2	line	Monk	He said I had no business spreading the word of Saradomin anywhere near his home. He said it was an affront to his order, whatever that means. He then threatened to get violent if I did it again!
2	line	Player	I see...
2	action	other
1	option	Have you seen anything odd around here lately?
2	line	Player	Have you seen anything odd around here lately?
2	line	Monk	No, I don't think so. Everything has been nice and quiet.
2	line	Player	No one acting suspicious at all? Or even just someone you didn't recognise?
2	line	Monk	No one at all. I'm very good at remembering people. It's an important part of my work.
2	line	Player	I see. Fair enough.
2	action	other
1	option	Actually, I'll be back later.
2	line	Player	Actually, I'll be back later.
2	line	Monk	Saradomin be with you.
2	action	end
1	option	That's all for now.
2	line	Player	That's all for now.
2	line	Monk	Saradomin be with you.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Joyce
1	line	Player	Hello there. I was wondering if I could ask you some questions?
1	line	Joyce	Questions? Yes, I suppose so.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Do you know anything about the person who lives in that house?
2	line	Player	Do you know anything about the person who lives in that house?
2	line	Joyce	Aye, that's the home of Bernard Holland. He's not the most social of people, but he's normally friendly enough. Always says hello when he heads out to tend to his onions.
2	line	Player	So he's a farmer as well then?
2	line	Joyce	Not like we are. I think for him it's more of a hobby. I seem to recall that he didn't always live around here. Shayzien is where he used to be from I think.
2	action	other
1	option	Have you seen anything odd around here lately?
2	line	Player	Have you seen anything odd around here lately?
2	line	Joyce	Odd? Like what?
2	line	Player	Maybe someone new passing through and acting suspicious, or something like that.
2	line	Joyce	Someone new? We don't get many new people coming through here. We're nice and out of the way. Typically it's just people heading past to go to the Tithe Farm.
2	action	other
1	option	Actually, I'll be back later.
2	line	Player	Actually, I'll be back later.
2	action	end
1	option	That's all for now.
2	line	Player	That's all for now.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Betty after finding all the clues
1	line	Betty	Have you found anything yet?
1	line	Player	Yes, I've found a few things that might be of note, but the main one is that I found some symbols, just like the ones back at your home.
1	line	Betty	Symbols? What do they mean?
1	line	Player	They seem to be part of some sort of cipher. There was also a letter back at your home that had the same symbols on it.
1	line	Betty	A cipher...? I don't understand. Why would the killer be doing this?
1	line	Player	I'm not sure, but it seems they want us to translate the letter. They're clearly intentionally leaving clues for how to do so.
1	line	Betty	But... if they're leaving clues, yet you don't have enough to translate the letter yet, that can only mean...
1	line	Player	They plan to strike again... if they haven't already. Betty, we need to get you to safety. We need to go to Sergeant Hudson.
1	line	Betty	No... We can't trust him! This kingdom is rotten to its core. It's the very thing my father spent so long fighting. We can't trust anyone of authority here.
1	line	Player	Surely there must be someone?
1	line	Betty	My father... he was good friends with a Shayzien captain, before they both retired. Captain Jensen is her name. She was one of the good ones. She can help us. I trust her.
1	line	Player	Hmm... Alright, where can we find her?
1	line	Betty	She lives in Port Piscarilius now.
1	line	Player	In that case, let's head over there. It's not safe for you to travel alone, so we'll go together.
1	line	Betty	Okay... Just let me know when you're ready to go.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Let's get going.
2	line	Player	Let's get going.
2	box	You depart for Port Piscarilius with Betty.
2	line	Sergeant Hudson	So here you are.
2	line	Player	Sergeant Hudson? What is this?
2	line	Sergeant Hudson	What this is, is the two of you now being suspects in a murder investigation. You were spotted at a crime scene, and yet you chose not to report what happened there.
2	line	Player	Hang on! We can explain!
2	line	Sergeant Hudson	I hope you can, and you will very much get your chance to do so. Corporal, find a cell for them in the local guardhouse. We'll question them once we're done here.
2	box	The corporal escorts you and Betty to a cell in the nearby guardhouse.
2	line	Betty	No, no, no! This can't be happening...
2	line	Betty	Can't those fools see what they're doing?! Something horrible is happening, and rather than doing anything about it, they just throw us in a cell instead!
2	line	Player	They're not wrong though. We did fail to report a murder to them.
2	line	Betty	With good reason!
2	line	Player	Well, let's hope we can explain that to them when they come to question us.
2	line	Betty	What? We can't just stay here! Don't you see? They were already here when we arrived! They can't have known where we were going. Something bad must have happened! We need to find out what!
2	line	Player	How? Betty, we're locked in a cell.
2	line	Betty	This is hardly the Shayzien Prison. These walls are rotting away! There must be a way through one of them.
2	line	Player	Perhaps, but breaking out of here is going to make us look even more guilty!
2	line	Betty	We don't have a choice. You need to get out of here, get over to Captain Jensen's house and then investigate whatever has happened there.
2	line	Player	And what about you?
2	line	Betty	I'll stay here. I can throw the guards off your scent if they find out you're gone. And if the killer is after me, I'll hopefully be a little bit safer here... for now at least.
2	line	Player	I don't like this, Betty, but alright. I'll see if I can find a way out.
2	action	end
1	option	I need to do something else first.
2	line	Player	I need to do something else first.
2	line	Betty	Okay... Just, please don't take too long.
2	action	end
