0	section	Shayzien
0	section	Approaching the war tent
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	Going somewhere?
1	line	Player	Sergeant Hudson! We need to act fast! I think the killer is targeting a Shayzien leader!
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	You flee one crime scene, arrive at another, then escape imprisonment, but now you expect me to listen to you? Why?
1	line	Player	I take it you saw the message left in that cell? Betty is missing!
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	Yes, and right now you're the prime suspect.
1	line	Player	We don't have time for this!
1	line	Corporal Breiman	Sergeant Hudson! Sergeant Hudson!
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	What is it, Corporal?
1	line	Corporal Breiman	It's not good, Sergeant. The killer has struck again!
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	Right, take this one to a cell. Make sure it's a bit more secure this time...
1	line	Corporal Breiman	I don't think it was [him/her/them], Sergeant. A hooded figure was spotted leaving the crime scene, literally just now!
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	An accomplice then... Sent here to cause a distraction for the killer so they could strike again.
1	line	Player	Sergeant, I know you don't trust me, but you have to believe me! I had nothing to do with any of this. I'm just trying to save Betty!
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	Then how did you know where the killer would be next?
1	line	Player	From the letter they left in Land's End. I managed to translate it. They wanted us to know. They've been toying with us the whole time!
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	You translated the letter? Curious...
1	line	Player	Please... let me help, Sergeant. We still have a chance to save Betty.
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	Hmm... Very well, but the Corporal here will be keeping a very close eye on you.
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	Who is the victim, Corporal?
1	line	Corporal Breiman	It's... It's the former Commissioner.
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	I see...
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	Come on then, let's get over there.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Sergeant Hudson
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	What a mess... Let's hope we can find something here that can lead us to the killer. I needn't remind you that if we can't, then you're still the prime suspect.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	What can you tell me about the victim?
2	line	Player	What can you tell me about the victim?
2	line	Sergeant Hudson	Commissioner Edwards. He led the Shayzien Constabulary for years, until he stepped down a couple of years ago. This is where he retired to.
2	line	Player	With a role like that, I'm guessing there are no shortages of possible suspects?
2	line	Sergeant Hudson	No. Every criminal in this kingdom would likely consider Edwards their enemy.
2	action	other
1	option	Did anything come from questioning that butcher?
2	line	Player	Did anything come from questioning that butcher?
2	line	Sergeant Hudson	No. All it did was confirm what we already knew. He had no obvious motive, and a butcher being in possession of a knife isn't enough evidence to mean anything.
2	action	other
1	option	Did you learn anything of note at the other crime scenes?
2	line	Player	Did you learn anything of note at the other crime scenes?
2	line	Sergeant Hudson	All manner of things, but none of them have led us to the killer yet.
2	line	Player	Anything you'd care to share?
2	line	Sergeant Hudson	No, but given you've been rather busy yourself, I'm guessing you know everything anyway.
2	action	other
1	option	What do you know about the Keystone Lodge?
2	line	Player	What do you know about the Keystone Lodge?
2	line	Sergeant Hudson	Not a lot. It was some secretive group, mostly made up of people of importance. Some called it a cult, others considered it nothing more than a drinking club.
2	line	Sergeant Hudson	And yes, I have already noticed that all of our victims were members of it.
2	action	other
1	option	Best I get to it then.
2	line	Player	Best I get to it then.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Corporal Campter
1	line	Corporal Campter	If it's any consolation, friend, I don't think you're guilty. Hopefully you understand that we can't be too careful though.
1	line	Player	I understand, and thank you.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Corporal Breiman
1	line	Corporal Breiman	Sorry, but I do need to keep an eye on you. Sergeant's orders.
1	line	Player	Fair enough.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Kyle
