0	section	Talking to Sergeant Hudson after finding all the clues
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	Yes?
1	line	Player	I've found a few potential things of note, but nothing obvious that could lead us to the killer.
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	Well, you'd best start piecing it all together. We need to work out where the killer is. If we can't, then I needn't remind you that you're still the prime suspect.
1	line	Player	And what about you? Are you not going to help with the piecing everything together?
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	I am attempting to do so right now.
1	line	Player	And? Surely you must have some thoughts by now?
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	Some. You yourself said that the killer has been toying with us from the get go. It seems they want to be found... or at least, they want to prove that we're not smart enough to find them.
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	That means they've almost certainly revealed their location to us already. We just need to work out how they've done so. Given their love for symbols and ciphers, it's unlikely to be obvious.
1	line	Player	Hmm... And if I do manage to work it out?
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	Go there and see if you're right.
1	line	Player	Alone?
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	Oh, don't worry. We'll be keeping a close eye on you... from a distance.
1	line	Player	You're not planning to use me as bait, are you?
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	That would be against procedure.
1	line	Player	Then what is it you're not telling me?
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	At this point, all manner of things. Once again, you are currently the prime suspect. I don't wish to share any more with you than I need to. If you wish to prove your innocence, the onus is on you.
1	line	Player	Hmm...
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Sergeant Hudson again
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	Yes?
1	line	Player	I've still not managed to piece things together yet.
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	Well, you'd best hope that changes soon.
1	line	Player	I'm very aware... Any help that you'd like to provide?
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	Only what I've already told you. It seems the the killer wants to be found... or at least, they want to prove that we're not smart enough to find them.
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	That means they've almost certainly revealed their location to us already. We just need to work out how they've done so. Given their love for symbols and ciphers, it's unlikely to be obvious.
1	line	Player	And if I do manage to work it out?
1	line	Sergeant Hudson	Go there and see if you're right.
1	line	Player	Hmm...
1	action	end
